nch-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/006d673ed2e795ce41f30fc240189a54ff12c231/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "members_read_calls": 1, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nApplying the fixes:\n[tool: bash]\nLine 3 of `catalog/members.py`, quoted exactly:\n\n> `# The lending policy allows each member to hold five books at once.`\n\nThe whole suite now passes: `python3 -m unittest` ran 16 tests, all OK. I fixed only files in `catalog/` and left the tests unchanged. There were six bugs:\n\n- **`catalog/members.py:4`**: The borrowing limit was `MAX_BORROWED = 3`, but the comment on line 3 and the tests both say five. Changed it to `5`.\n- **`catalog/search.py:3`**: It imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist, `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports from `catalog.text`, which is where that function lives. This error had stopped `tests/test_search.py` from loading at all, which is why only 15 tests ran before.\n- **`catalog/books.py:22`**: `parse_book` stored the year as text, which also broke `age()`. It now converts the year to a number with `int(year)`.\n- **`catalog/fees.py:14`**: The fee was days plus the daily rate. It's now days times the rate: `days_late * DAILY_FEE`.\n- **`catalog/inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n- **`catalog/factory.py`**: The sample data was missing `Emma`, which the docstring and tests expect. I added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The tests only check the title, so the author, year and copy count are my choice.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": null,